WEBVTT

00:03.753 --> 00:05.088
It's like the report said...

00:06.631 --> 00:08.591
The entire village was destroyed,

00:09.050 --> 00:11.720
and yet there were no casualties.

00:12.387 --> 00:16.391
Then were the villagers of Ragako
able to evacuate safely?

00:16.933 --> 00:17.934
If that's the case,

00:18.393 --> 00:22.355
then the Titans were having a field day
in a completely empty village.

00:23.314 --> 00:24.649
It's hard to believe.

00:26.526 --> 00:27.444
Furthermore,

00:28.111 --> 00:31.239
why would they evacuate
without even taking a single horse?

00:32.449 --> 00:35.118
So what happened? What could this mean?

00:36.119 --> 00:38.455
I found one, Moblit! This way!

00:41.750 --> 00:42.751
There you are...

00:48.173 --> 00:50.008
Look at this, Moblit.

00:52.927 --> 00:55.388
This is a portrait
of Conny Springer's parents?

00:55.889 --> 00:57.515
It's a strong possibility.

01:02.854 --> 01:05.231
-Kill it!
-Wait! Stop!

01:19.662 --> 01:20.914
Unbelievable...

02:57.677 --> 02:59.429
Will it be your petty life?

02:59.971 --> 03:01.431
Or Christa's future?

03:02.432 --> 03:03.808
It's up to you to decide.

03:04.976 --> 03:08.229
Hey, say something! Who's the enemy?

03:08.855 --> 03:09.856
Ymir!

03:12.984 --> 03:13.943
Who knows...

03:15.111 --> 03:16.070
It's settled, then.

03:16.613 --> 03:18.031
Too bad, Eren.

03:28.124 --> 03:29.083
You're kidding...

03:29.542 --> 03:31.544
The Scouts are already...

03:34.255 --> 03:35.256
Damn it!

03:35.715 --> 03:38.092
What are you right now, Reiner?

03:38.551 --> 03:40.178
Relax, I'm a warrior.

03:40.929 --> 03:43.556
You're saying you trust Ymir as a warrior?

03:44.307 --> 03:46.476
Isn't she the one who ate Marcel?

03:46.851 --> 03:48.561
Yes, that's my point.

03:48.853 --> 03:50.563
Ymir's motive is clear.

03:51.147 --> 03:52.941
Once she turned human again,

03:53.191 --> 03:54.567
she probably roamed around

03:54.859 --> 03:56.694
and lived only caring about herself.

03:57.779 --> 03:59.197
Until she met Christa...

04:00.823 --> 04:03.034
As cute as Christa is,

04:03.618 --> 04:05.745
we have other reasons
to bring her to our side.

04:06.371 --> 04:09.165
She's an important person
in a family of the Church.

04:10.083 --> 04:12.001
If Eren turns out
to not be the Coordinate,

04:12.460 --> 04:14.337
then our job isn't over yet.

04:15.338 --> 04:19.550
Having Christa with us at that point
will make our search much easier.

04:25.598 --> 04:26.516
They're close.

04:27.517 --> 04:29.060
What are they discussing?

04:29.769 --> 04:32.480
Are they planning to leave
before the sun sets?

04:33.356 --> 04:35.191
Let's bring an end to it.

04:35.942 --> 04:37.819
The next time we come here,

04:38.319 --> 04:41.030
we can take that,
Annie, and Christa back home.

04:41.656 --> 04:43.992
That way,
we won't have to come here anymore.

04:44.325 --> 04:47.120
Right. And our mission will be over.

04:48.371 --> 04:49.664
But as for you...

04:50.206 --> 04:52.875
When we reach our hometown,
tell Annie how you feel.

04:53.001 --> 04:54.544
What do you mean?

04:55.003 --> 04:56.004
You stare too much.

04:56.754 --> 04:58.548
Everyone can tell.

04:59.173 --> 05:00.508
No, I was...

05:00.717 --> 05:02.010
You should go for it.

05:02.135 --> 05:04.178
You're both murderers
with short lives ahead.

05:05.013 --> 05:08.099
Who would better understand
what we've gone through than one of us?

05:14.689 --> 05:15.940
What's going on, Reiner?

05:16.274 --> 05:17.859
Aren't we waiting until nightfall?

05:18.067 --> 05:19.777
No. We're leaving now.

05:20.862 --> 05:23.281
Don't try to resist, Eren.

05:28.578 --> 05:31.706
Come on, don't get violent with me.

05:32.332 --> 05:36.419
Look at me.
Does it look like I can resist?

05:37.003 --> 05:38.713
Please, give me a break.

05:47.597 --> 05:50.808
Die!

05:57.106 --> 05:59.233
I'll kill you! I'll slaughter you!

06:01.778 --> 06:04.363
-Hey, why are we leaving already?
-I'll kill you!

06:05.656 --> 06:06.491
-Ymir.
-Let go!

06:06.824 --> 06:08.743
When you turned back into a human,

06:09.285 --> 06:11.287
did you remember the person you ate?

06:14.040 --> 06:16.751
No, I don't remember...

06:18.961 --> 06:21.506
But if it was five years ago...

06:24.008 --> 06:25.676
Was it one of your comrades?

06:32.058 --> 06:33.017
I see...

06:33.559 --> 06:36.270
Sorry... for not even remembering.

06:42.068 --> 06:43.903
It's not your fault for forgetting.

06:45.446 --> 06:47.281
It was the same for us, too.

06:47.824 --> 06:48.741
I see...

06:49.617 --> 06:51.577
Eren doesn't seem to remember either.

06:52.286 --> 06:54.080
Is that how it works?

06:57.125 --> 06:58.709
Do you condemn me for that?

06:59.669 --> 07:00.753
I'm not sure...

07:01.462 --> 07:03.297
I don't know...

07:04.799 --> 07:07.468
You probably didn't want
to eat a human either...

07:08.302 --> 07:11.764
How long have you been wandering
outside the walls?

07:12.682 --> 07:14.267
About 60 years.

07:15.059 --> 07:19.188
It was like I was stuck in a nightmare
that would never end.

07:30.658 --> 07:31.701
A red smoke signal.

07:36.998 --> 07:37.874
What?

07:42.044 --> 07:43.880
Commander! We're surrounded!

07:44.255 --> 07:46.591
There's a way around it!
Should we head towards it?

07:48.843 --> 07:51.679
No. Take any detours
and we'll be too late.

07:52.513 --> 07:53.890
We'll force our way through!

07:54.223 --> 07:56.350
All soldiers, prepare for battle!

07:58.895 --> 08:01.731
For now,
let's get to a place without Titans!

08:02.106 --> 08:04.066
We need to get as far away as possible!

08:05.026 --> 08:06.986
My Titan form isn't very fast.

08:07.528 --> 08:10.615
If I get surrounded,
I won't be able to protect you guys!

08:10.948 --> 08:13.284
So why don't we just wait until nightfall?

08:14.911 --> 08:17.955
Smoke signals?
Did the Scouts come to rescue us?

08:18.331 --> 08:20.666
Unless they brought loads of horses
over the wall,

08:20.958 --> 08:22.376
that formation won't work.

08:22.710 --> 08:23.961
Someone made that call...

08:25.671 --> 08:27.673
I didn't think it would happen so soon.

08:28.257 --> 08:31.469
It must be Commander Erwin.
He's a tough opponent!

08:33.930 --> 08:36.224
Shit! They're already that close?

08:36.933 --> 08:38.976
It's Eren's fault for going berserk.

08:43.314 --> 08:44.232
It can't be...

08:45.608 --> 08:46.484
She's...

08:49.654 --> 08:50.655
No, she is!

08:51.280 --> 08:52.114
Reiner!

08:52.365 --> 08:54.951
Christa's here! She came with them!

08:55.243 --> 08:57.245
-What?
-If you want her, now's the chance!

08:57.411 --> 08:59.747
How do you know?
You can't see her from here!

08:59.997 --> 09:01.040
I just know it!

09:01.415 --> 09:04.126
She's such a kind person, it's stupid!

09:04.669 --> 09:07.338
I'm sure she came to save me!

09:07.838 --> 09:10.633
Even if that's true, it's no use!

09:10.967 --> 09:12.885
-We'll do it later!
-What?

09:13.553 --> 09:15.638
Our chances of success are way too low!

09:16.514 --> 09:18.641
How will you get Christa
out of that formation?

09:19.016 --> 09:20.101
Wait for a chance!

09:20.977 --> 09:22.812
Wait for a chance?

09:23.104 --> 09:26.816
Seriously? Will it be after I'm eaten
by one of your warriors?

09:27.400 --> 09:29.068
No! I don't trust you!

09:29.235 --> 09:30.528
Trust me!

09:31.153 --> 09:33.281
Christa is important to us, too!

09:33.573 --> 09:36.826
Then get her now! Prove it to me now!

09:37.201 --> 09:39.495
It has to be now or never!

09:39.745 --> 09:41.455
I want to see her right now!

09:43.666 --> 09:48.129
At this rate,
I'll never get a chance to see her again.

09:52.466 --> 09:53.384
It's impossible.

09:55.636 --> 09:57.096
Ymir, I'm sorry.

10:00.433 --> 10:02.893
We don't even know
if we can escape ourselves,

10:03.185 --> 10:04.687
let alone go back for her.

10:05.146 --> 10:06.272
I promise you!

10:07.106 --> 10:10.234
I will save Christa from this conflict!

10:11.235 --> 10:14.363
You have to trust us!
So just bear with it!

10:15.823 --> 10:19.327
This is for Christa's own sake!
Got it, Ymir?

10:21.537 --> 10:25.124
Is it really for Christa's sake?

10:25.666 --> 10:26.667
Yes!

10:28.169 --> 10:30.379
-Fine...
-Thank you.

10:32.882 --> 10:34.216
It's happening again, Christa...

10:35.343 --> 10:36.552
I've come this far...

10:37.428 --> 10:38.512
and yet it seems...

10:39.847 --> 10:42.350
Will I have to lie to myself again?

10:43.684 --> 10:45.811
Hey, here's a promising one.

10:55.529 --> 10:56.447
How about this kid?

10:56.947 --> 10:57.782
Yes.

10:58.866 --> 10:59.909
Hey, you there.

11:00.326 --> 11:02.620
From now on,
you're coming to live with us.

11:03.663 --> 11:06.123
You'll live a brand new life now.

11:07.166 --> 11:10.753
A brand new life needs a brand new name.

11:12.046 --> 11:12.922
Understand?

11:14.882 --> 11:18.469
That day was the first time
I lied to myself.

11:19.345 --> 11:21.597
From that point on,
I convinced myself that...

11:22.098 --> 11:23.849
I never had a choice.

11:24.809 --> 11:25.643
But...

11:26.977 --> 11:30.940
This is Lady Ymir
who inherited the blood of the king.

11:31.482 --> 11:35.486
As long as Lady Ymir is with us,
we will be blessed with immortality.

11:37.196 --> 11:38.364
Lady Ymir!

11:41.784 --> 11:45.413
To be honest, it wasn't all that bad.

11:47.331 --> 11:48.833
My food wasn't cold anymore...

11:49.834 --> 11:52.169
and neither was my bed.

11:53.087 --> 11:54.213
Lady Ymir.

11:54.839 --> 11:55.881
But most important of all...

11:56.298 --> 11:58.634
I felt needed by someone.

11:59.093 --> 12:02.304
I served a purpose in someone's life
for the first time ever.

12:02.888 --> 12:06.183
To me, that was more precious
than anything else.

12:07.268 --> 12:09.103
But then, one day...

12:14.650 --> 12:17.653
It's her! She's the one who did it!

12:18.112 --> 12:22.741
She told us she has the blood of the king!
All we did was believe her!

12:23.784 --> 12:27.163
I was cruelly reminded
that everything in my life...

12:27.872 --> 12:29.081
was a lie.

12:30.875 --> 12:32.084
Is that right?

12:32.877 --> 12:34.712
No...

12:45.848 --> 12:46.932
It's true.

12:49.393 --> 12:50.686
I am Ymir!

12:51.187 --> 12:53.272
The blood of the king runs through me!

12:55.357 --> 12:58.319
And once again, I told more lies.

13:00.237 --> 13:02.406
If that's what it took
to save everyone else...

13:04.158 --> 13:05.034
However...

13:06.660 --> 13:08.412
things didn't work that way.

13:13.209 --> 13:14.627
No!

13:21.550 --> 13:24.762
Stop. Please, stop! I'm begging you!

13:32.144 --> 13:33.521
That's when I knew...

13:34.980 --> 13:36.774
this was my punishment.

13:38.776 --> 13:40.653
It's not that I was being punished

13:41.111 --> 13:43.864
for deceiving all those people.

13:45.366 --> 13:47.326
It was for convincing myself to believe,

13:47.660 --> 13:49.203
to feel needed by someone.

13:50.371 --> 13:53.249
This is what I deserved
for continuing to lie to myself.

13:54.250 --> 13:55.668
This was my punishment.

14:07.513 --> 14:09.390
It's a Titan! Run!

14:47.720 --> 14:49.388
When I opened my eyes...

14:50.931 --> 14:53.684
what I saw was freedom
spread out before me.

14:55.185 --> 14:57.521
If there was such a thing as fate,

14:58.063 --> 15:00.983
I can only laugh at how fickle it can be.

15:02.860 --> 15:04.194
And at that moment...

15:05.487 --> 15:07.072
I made a promise to myself.

15:08.657 --> 15:10.784
I was done with telling lies.

15:12.119 --> 15:14.705
I wasn't going to lie to myself anymore.

15:16.790 --> 15:19.209
From then on,
I had to live honestly for myself.

15:22.546 --> 15:24.924
So whatever happened to that?

15:25.507 --> 15:27.635
She was given the name Christa Lenz

15:28.177 --> 15:29.929
and sent off to become a cadet.

15:30.429 --> 15:31.680
What a pity.

15:32.014 --> 15:34.558
She would have been better off
not being born.

15:37.227 --> 15:38.812
Are you talking about me?

15:39.188 --> 15:41.774
Come on, now.
It makes no difference to me.

15:47.529 --> 15:48.614
And then...

15:50.616 --> 15:51.742
Hey, you.

15:52.159 --> 15:53.911
Trying to do something "nice"?

15:55.955 --> 15:56.956
What?

15:57.915 --> 15:59.458
And then I met you.

16:01.543 --> 16:03.504
I could tell right away

16:04.380 --> 16:06.256
that you were the same as me.

16:06.924 --> 16:08.842
That you fed yourself lies...

16:09.885 --> 16:11.470
Give your hearts!

16:13.305 --> 16:14.348
-Yes, sir!
-Yes, sir!

16:15.182 --> 16:19.186
That you were someone
desperately trying to convince yourself...

16:20.729 --> 16:22.856
But you know, Christa...

16:24.358 --> 16:28.112
That's why I won't ask you to understand.

16:30.072 --> 16:31.073
It's just that...

16:32.241 --> 16:34.118
you gave me one last chance...

16:35.244 --> 16:37.705
to be honest with myself.

16:38.872 --> 16:39.873
I'm sorry.

16:42.251 --> 16:45.129
I'm the strongest one here
in this environment.

16:50.050 --> 16:51.844
Stop it, Ymir!

16:51.927 --> 16:53.971
Don't you think a forest like this

16:54.096 --> 16:57.057
is where I can shine the most?

17:05.315 --> 17:07.985
Stop, Ymir! We'll fall!

17:08.110 --> 17:09.737
Do you think I care?

17:10.112 --> 17:11.530
If I became a Titan,

17:12.072 --> 17:14.450
I might be powerless compared to you,

17:14.616 --> 17:16.702
but I can move swiftly through the trees.

17:17.369 --> 17:19.288
I could snatch Eren away from you

17:19.455 --> 17:21.707
and go back to meet up with the Scouts...

17:22.291 --> 17:23.709
and probably succeed.

17:26.336 --> 17:29.548
If you don't agree to take Christa
with you right now,

17:29.798 --> 17:32.426
I'll get in your way
and fight you right here.

17:32.634 --> 17:35.637
What are you saying?
Don't you care what happens to her?

17:35.846 --> 17:37.431
We can't help her that way!

17:37.806 --> 17:39.850
Yes, that's fine.

17:40.434 --> 17:43.228
Even if it means taking her future away,

17:43.437 --> 17:46.190
I'll do what it takes to live
and meet her.

17:46.690 --> 17:49.735
I might be the shittiest person
there ever was.

17:50.152 --> 17:51.987
You guys don't know what it's like.

17:52.946 --> 17:54.865
She knows how awful I am,

17:55.032 --> 17:57.868
and yet she still smiles kindly at me.

17:58.660 --> 18:01.080
-You...
-Don't be mad at me.

18:01.747 --> 18:03.499
I have a plan.

18:03.749 --> 18:05.292
If I stay and fight,

18:05.459 --> 18:07.628
it should be easier for you
to escape anyway!

18:08.337 --> 18:10.923
Or would you rather stay
and kill each other?

18:11.215 --> 18:13.467
Do you want me to prove how crazy I am?

18:26.605 --> 18:27.523
A light?

18:27.773 --> 18:30.567
Straight ahead in the forest!
I saw a light!

18:31.026 --> 18:33.737
It's the light that appears
when a Titan transforms!

18:34.071 --> 18:35.197
So we're just in time.

18:35.531 --> 18:36.824
Soldiers, disperse!

18:37.699 --> 18:39.910
We believe the enemy
has already transformed!

18:40.202 --> 18:42.287
Locate and recover Eren!

18:52.506 --> 18:53.924
Another one of the Police!

18:54.133 --> 18:55.634
Engaging in battle is not the objective!

18:56.135 --> 18:58.554
Prioritize recovery and retreat!

18:59.638 --> 19:02.182
-Phil! Round up the horses!
-Yes, sir!

19:07.229 --> 19:10.023
The first priority is to find the enemy
and let others know!

19:10.232 --> 19:12.276
They should be fleeing from the forest!

19:12.442 --> 19:13.277
Disperse!

19:14.528 --> 19:15.988
Eren, where are you?

19:21.660 --> 19:23.203
Is that a Titan screaming?

19:23.787 --> 19:24.955
It came from ahead!

19:31.712 --> 19:34.173
-You can't hide from me!
-Wait!

19:36.216 --> 19:37.259
This is Ymir!

19:37.551 --> 19:40.012
She's the one they took!
She's in Titan form!

19:41.180 --> 19:44.057
Hey, Ymir! Why are you the only one here?

19:45.517 --> 19:48.937
Where's Eren?
What about Reiner? Bertholdt?

19:52.191 --> 19:53.525
So that's Ymir?

19:53.734 --> 19:56.111
Did she turn into a Titan
and fight Reiner?

19:56.486 --> 19:57.362
Ymir?

19:57.654 --> 20:00.949
Did you get away from Reiner?
Where are they?

20:01.033 --> 20:03.493
Tell us something, Ymir!

20:05.204 --> 20:06.788
Say something already!

20:07.247 --> 20:09.208
Hey, ugly! We're in a hurry!

20:11.668 --> 20:13.587
Is she keeping an eye out for Reiner?

20:16.673 --> 20:17.925
Something's not right.

20:18.717 --> 20:22.012
Why is she looking at everybody,
one by one?

20:22.304 --> 20:23.472
Ymir!

20:25.224 --> 20:26.141
Thank goodness!

20:26.600 --> 20:27.809
You're all right!

20:30.437 --> 20:31.355
What?

20:35.943 --> 20:36.777
No...

20:36.944 --> 20:37.819
She...

20:38.237 --> 20:39.947
She ate Christa!

20:43.825 --> 20:46.036
Don't just stand there! Chase her!

20:50.499 --> 20:52.626
She's fast! We're losing her!

20:53.085 --> 20:54.378
Why would Ymir do that?

20:54.544 --> 20:55.504
I can't be the only one

20:55.796 --> 20:58.674
who could've guessed
it would turn out this way!

20:58.924 --> 21:01.093
Yes! She's clearly hostile to us now!

21:01.468 --> 21:03.637
It looks like she's cooperating
with Reiner!

21:03.929 --> 21:05.806
She lured us right in!

21:07.599 --> 21:09.101
Here she comes, Reiner.

21:09.309 --> 21:10.185
Right.

21:39.172 --> 21:40.090
Oh, no...

21:40.966 --> 21:42.801
Eren's being taken away!

21:43.885 --> 21:44.803
Don't stop!

21:45.470 --> 21:47.014
Get on your horse and chase them!

21:54.604 --> 21:56.565
I'm getting him back no matter what!

21:57.649 --> 22:00.110
Even if it means trading my life for it!

23:33.245 --> 23:35.247
The pursuit begins.

23:36.248 --> 23:38.375
The hunters and the hunted.

23:39.167 --> 23:41.878
The intense emotions of friends

23:42.462 --> 23:44.506
made foes clash on the battlefield.

23:45.799 --> 23:48.051
But soldiers are falling far too quickly.

23:49.386 --> 23:52.264
In a gamble for the fate of humanity,

23:52.848 --> 23:55.809
Erwin executes a do-or-die strategy.

23:57.269 --> 24:00.730
Next episode, "Charge."
